2608a13fc76b41f1570d465194557403a096ab6e","position":"1788896451359175001-d27c025f-8afd-45af-b331-69466eccbaa8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4d54824dd60a492159bf00421a4487ed030fe389592f1d6200332b3d3aa63a0d","event_uuid":"8c0f817f-5de3-4e6f-8867-980fdd613088","position":{"commit_sha":"6a54484dcd3df4c26065c7e91b92787e96ae5d44","position":"1788896718705482869-8c0f817f-5de3-4e6f-8867-980fdd613088"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Live trajectory for this metric, measured tonight, relevant to the arithmetic question this ticket raises.\n\n`docker_unaccounted_bytes` across the operator-authorised `systemctl restart docker` at 05:23 UTC:\n\n    2.84 GB   before the restart          (alarm firing)\n    1.42 GB   immediately after           (alarm CLEARED -- real orphan sweep)\n    1.89 GB   steady for ~45 min\n    2.81 GB   at 00:58 PDT                (alarm firing again)\n\nSo the restart genuinely reclaimed ~1.4 GB, and the figure then climbed back over the 2 GiB threshold within about an hour and a half.\n\n## Why this bears on THIS ticket rather than being a separate finding\n\nThis ticket's claim is that the metric `subtracts apparent-size ledger rows from an allocated-size total` — i.e. that the number mixes two different notions of size (`du -sx` allocated blocks versus `docker system df` apparent sizes). If that is right, then part of the 2.81 GB is an ARTEFACT of the arithmetic rather than genuine unreachable residue, and the growth rate above is not a clean measurement of anything.\n\nI am deliberately NOT drawing the obvious conclusion. Two readings fit the same numbers:\n\n- **(a)** orphaned overlay2 really is re-accumulating fast (~0.9 GB in one 15-minute bucket), which would make the restart a temporary reprieve and point at whatever generator is producing it; or\n- **(b)** the arithmetic overstates, and the post-restart 1.42 GB / 1.89 GB baseline is closer to a floor of measurement error than to real residue.\n\nDistinguishing them needs the ground truth this ticket is about: `du -sx --block-size=1` over `/var/lib/docker/overlay2` compared against the ledger sum, on the box, at one instant. Until that is done, the number should not be used to size a remediation.\n\nOne caveat on the step from 1.89 to 2.81 GB: a ~0.9 GB jump inside a single 15-minute bucket is more consistent with a discrete event (an image pull, a build, a container write) than with steady accrual. Worth identifying before assuming a leak.\n\nRecording the series so whoever fixes the arithmetic has a real trace to validate against — a corrected metric should be able to explain these six points, not just produce a different number.","timestamp":1788596124591264001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Live demonstration of this defect from another session: a reclaim that improved the filesystem by 4.93 GB made `docker_unaccounted_bytes` **4.75 GB worse**. The metric moved decisively in the wrong direction.\n\n**What was done.** `docker builder prune -f` on the production host at ~10:55 UTC, 2026-09-05. Measured immediately before and after with `df -k /` and `docker system df` on the box:\n\n    BEFORE   /dev/nvme0n1p1  62837740  45189568  17648172  72% /\n             Build Cache  107 entries  0 ACTIVE  5.877GB  5.877GB RECLAIMABLE\n\n    AFTER    /dev/nvme0n1p1  62837740  40263832  22573908  65% /\n             Build Cache   25 entries  0 ACTIVE  0B       0B\n\nReal bytes freed on the filesystem: **4,925,736 KB = 4.93 GB**, seven percentage points of root.\n\n**What the metric did.** `docker_unaccounted_bytes` went from ~3.79e9 before to **8.54e9 after** — up ~4.75 GB.\n\n**Why, and why it is exactly this ticket's defect.** The metric is `du -sx --block-size=1 /var/lib/docker` (ALLOCATED BLOCKS) minus the four `docker system df` rows (APPARENT sizes). The prune removed 5.877 GB from the LEDGER — the subtrahend — but only 4.93 GB from the disk, the minuend's basis. A ~0.95 GB gap opens immediately, and it opens in the direction that inflates \"unaccounted\", on top of the ~12.4% structural inflation this ticket already documents.\n\nSo the arithmetic is not merely imprecise: **a genuine, successful, 100%-reclaimable cleanup registers as a large regression** in the metric whose name claims to measure bytes no prune can reach. That is close to the inverse of its stated purpose, and it will now keep `rebar-docker-unaccounted-bytes` (threshold 2 GiB) alarming harder than before the host got healthier.\n\n**Operator consequence, since that is what makes this worth a comment rather than a footnote.** An operator watching this metric would read the post-prune value as evidence the prune failed or made things worse, and could reasonably escalate to something more destructive — a `system prune`, an image purge — chasing 8.54 GB of \"unaccounted\" bytes that are substantially an accounting artifact. The correct reading required going to `df` and `docker system df` directly, which is precisely what this ticket says the metric should have spared us.\n\n**Not claiming this is the whole gap.** ~0.95 GB is the ledger-vs-disk discrepancy from this one operation; the rest of the 8.54 GB includes the xfs block-allocation overhead already quantified here (56% of the residue in the earlier measurement) plus whatever genuinely un-ledgered content exists. I did not re-derive the split post-prune.\n\nRecording as evidence only; no action taken on this ticket. Related: `undefiled-revivable-gemsbok` covers the sibling defect where `docker_buildkit_cache_used_percent` is clamped at 100 and so could not show that the same cache was 9% OVER its 5.00 GiB budget before this prune.","timestamp":1788606605830591152},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-06: alarm work APPROVED — mirror existing alarm best practices in this environment; every alarm must provide meaningful health signal, not noise.","timestamp":1788830966445639001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Skipping per workflow after second plan-review failure. Verbatim blocking findings from retry: E4 — The plan's fix ('Change the residue's minuend ONLY to apparent size' while 'Leave docker_storage_bytes on ALLOCATED blocks') assumes the two are separable, but in the code both are the SAME single value: docker_total_bytes = DOCKER_DU_TOTAL from one census walk that feeds docker_storage_bytes and the residue subtraction. G1G2/T3/G6 — the plan must specify how to obtain both allocated blocks for docker_storage_bytes and apparent size for residue without a second Docker-root du walk, because a single du invocation reports one size semantic and a second walk reintroduces bug 9313's timeout regression. Required resolution: revise plan to name the mechanism (or explicitly accept/update the single-walk budget/tests) before claim/implementation.","timestamp":1788832372482716001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review now PASS after revising the design to use one find/stat metadata traversal for allocated+apparent Docker-root sizes and explicitly updating the bug-9313 timeout assertions. Starting implementation in a separate worktree.","timestamp":1788892806017986001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 2845 (PS1) at 2026-09-08T19:34:43Z. Verification before push: targeted pytest for observability docker storage + timeout suites passed (44 tests), terraform alarm tests passed (19), docker storage cap tests passed (25), make lint passed, and full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=8 passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset. Waiting for LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1788896088347095001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2845 still has no LLM-Review or Verified labels after initial wait; unresolved comments remain 0. I am holding push-and-wait discipline and checking CI/review-bot status before any further push.","timestamp":1788896451359175001}],"created_at":1788570676986381001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8c0f817f-5de3-4e6f-8867-980fdd613088","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2356-b4c9-73e2-4009"}],"description":"## Defect\n\n`docker_unaccounted_bytes` subtracts Docker-ledger apparent sizes from a Docker-root filesystem total measured as allocated blocks. Those units are not commensurable, so XFS allocation overhead appears as unreachable Docker residue. On 2026-09-05 the host measurement was:\n\n- allocated Docker root: 13,642,739,712 bytes\n- apparent Docker root: 12,140,814,875 bytes\n- Docker ledger: 10,957,600,000 bytes\n\nThe current calculation reports 2,685,139,712 bytes unaccounted. The commensurable apparent-size residue is 1,183,214,875 bytes. The sibling `docker_storage_bytes` metric must remain allocated-block based because it reports real disk consumption.\n\n## Design\n\nReplace the Docker-root filesystem census with one metadata pass that returns both sizes:\n\n- allocated bytes = sum of `st_blocks * 512`, preserving `docker_storage_bytes`;\n- apparent bytes = sum of `st_size`, used only as the minuend for `docker_unaccounted_bytes`;\n- overlay2 breadcrumb = accumulated allocated bytes for paths under the overlay2 subtree;\n- hardlinks are de-duplicated by device+inode so allocated/apparent totals retain `du`-like semantics;\n- the pass stays inside the Docker root filesystem (`find -xdev`) and keeps the existing overlay2 cross-device guard.\n\nThis avoids the rejected second `du` walk from bug 9313: one traversal emits all filesystem quantities, and `docker system df` is still called once for the Docker ledger and container rows. The implementation will update the bug-9313 regression tests that currently assert the single Docker-root walk is specifically a `du --max-depth=1` invocation; after this change those tests must assert the same timeout invariant in find/stat terms (one Docker-root filesystem walk, no overlay2-only second walk, bounded command shape). No threshold raise and no prune action are part of this fix.\n\n## Affected files\n\n- `infra/scripts/observability.sh`\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_docker_storage.py`\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_timeout_9313.py`\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf`\n- `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md`\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `docker_storage_bytes` remains allocated-block based, while `docker_unaccounted_bytes` subtracts the Docker ledger from apparent Docker-root bytes.\n- [ ] AC2: a defect-seeded test replays allocated=13,642,739,712, apparent=12,140,814,875, ledger=10,957,600,000 and expects `docker_unaccounted_bytes=1,183,214,875`; the old allocated-minus-ledger value would fail.\n- [ ] AC3: the implementation obtains allocated and apparent Docker-root sizes from one filesystem traversal, not two `du` walks or root+overlay2 walks.\n- [ ] AC4: the bug-9313 timeout regression is updated from `du --max-depth=1` shape checks to equivalent single-walk find/stat assertions.\n- [ ] AC5: the alarm rationale records the measured baseline and corrects the old “hundreds of MB” assumption without raising the threshold.\n- [ ] AC6: the runbook guidance distinguishes allocation overhead from genuine unaccounted content and does not overstate container JSON logs/buildkit/image as the usual source.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun `pytest tests/scripts/test_observability_docker_storage.py tests/scripts/test_observability_timeout_9313.py -q`, any touched Terraform/runbook tests, `make lint`, and full `make verify` with the required `GIT_CONFIG_*` unsets before push.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"Compute docker_unaccounted_bytes from an apparent-size Docker root census while leaving docker_storage_bytes allocated-block based."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_observability_docker_storage.py","reason":"Defect-seeded tests for allocated-vs-apparent residue using the production measurements."},{"path":"infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf","reason":"Correct the Docker unaccounted alarm threshold rationale to the measured apparent-size baseline without changing the threshold."},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"Correct the runbook's unaccounted-byte subtree guidance so it no longer overstates container JSON logs/buildkit/image as the usual sources."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2356-b4c9-73e2-4009"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8f0dacbd-1a43-4b0e-aaa5-c0045243d6e3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"81cc-bced-62f4-40b9","ticket_type":"bug","title":"docker_unaccounted_bytes subtracts apparent-size ledger rows from an allocated-blocks du, so 56% of today's 2.5 GiB residue is xfs block overhead and the alarm will fire from rounding before the host reaches its own budget","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c497d99b-20ef-4f25-9314-3ddcc353aad3","9f0619c4-b4f3-4117-a9fb-f94733d6c1e3","ccb1adde-4919-40db-aa57-098c8592390e","6c7370ed-f837-41fd-a5b5-ebf2a078389f","c010bdd7-6331-4bd4-96d7-41531380727b","0ce9eafd-9f07-4d43-8589-091593e78c18","5a0e3dd2-a83c-4122-9d6b-47e91d419e66","06e213d4-49ed-413e-af4d-ea4be54eb935","35e2ec2c-8b57-490c-99b0-84c143cb57b0","8f0dacbd-1a43-4b0e-aaa5-c0045243d6e3","4d394a2e-0b0c-4244-9b53-5ee5ccf569db","67f369be-5820-461a-8f1d-718510be92b3","705e62aa-098d-449c-8dc2-e06c50840f26","d27c025f-8afd-45af-b331-69466eccbaa8","8c0f817f-5de3-4e6f-8867-980fdd613088"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788896718705482870,"uuid":"e96138df-1274-4720-8de4-7ec9e93607d9"}